  "summary": "Give your opinion with فِي رَأْيِي and أَعْتَقِدُ أَنَّ…, ask other people what they think, and agree or disagree politely.",
  "intro": "Mr Karim starts a class debate: is the internet better than books? To give an opinion, begin with فِي رَأْيِي (in my opinion), or say أَعْتَقِدُ أَنَّ… (I believe that…) or أَظُنُّ أَنَّ… (I think that…). As you know, after أَنَّ the noun ends in -a. Ask مَا رَأْيُكَ؟ (what do you think?), agree with أُوَافِقُ or مَعَكَ حَقّ (you're right), and disagree politely with مَعَ احْتِرَامِي، لَا أُوَافِقُ (with respect, I don't agree).",
  "objectives": [
    "Give an opinion with فِي رَأْيِي and أَعْتَقِدُ أَنَّ…",
    "Ask a man, a woman or a group what they think",
    "Agree with أُوَافِقُ and مَعَكَ حَقّ, and disagree politely",
    "Say that something is important, useful or a mistake"
  ],
